# slashmem — AI agent memory rules
#
# Copy this file into any project root to integrate slashmem with your AI
# workflow. Agents that read CLAUDE.md / .cursorrules / similar config files
# will pick up these instructions automatically.

## Before starting work

Before writing any code, retrieve relevant memories for the current task:

```bash
sm context "<brief task description>"
```

Review the returned procedural rules, recent episodes, and working-memory
entries. Use them to avoid past mistakes and follow established patterns.

## After finishing work

Once the task is complete (code written, tests passing), record what happened:

```bash
sm ingest --task "<task-id>" --agent "<agent-name>" --body "<what was done and any lessons learned>"
```

If a procedural rule helped you succeed, reinforce it:

```bash
sm ingest --task "<task-id>" --agent "<agent-name>" --body "<summary>" --success "<rule-id>"
```

If following a rule caused problems, signal that:

```bash
sm ingest --task "<task-id>" --agent "<agent-name>" --body "<summary>" --harm "<rule-id>"
```

## Periodic maintenance

Run distillation periodically to decay stale confidence, promote mature
working-memory entries, and prune low-value records:

```bash
sm distill
```
